---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import RecipeList from "../../components/RecipeList.astro";

// The gluten-free shelf. Not a third book — a cut across both, since a
// gluten-free dish may be fasting or not. Open to anyone, like the
// fasting book: signed out it shows the gluten-free fasting recipes,
// and a sign-in adds the everyday ones.
---

<Layout
  title="Gluten-Free Recipes | An Orthodox Table"
  description="Gluten-free recipes — fasting and everyday — shared by St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Mission."
>
  <RecipeList
    book="gluten-free"
    heading="Gluten-Free Recipes"
    blurb="From both books, fasting and everyday. Each one was marked gluten-free by the person who shared it, and read over before it went up."
  />

  <!-- Said plainly and said once. The people who need this page have
       coeliac disease or something near it, and the thing that catches
       them out is never the flour — it is the stock cube. A parish
       collection cannot verify a brand, so it should not pretend to. -->
  <aside class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-5xl px-4 md:px-6">
    <div class="border-l-2 border-sacred-gold bg-cream-card p-5">
      <h2 class="font-display text-base text-text-primary">Please still check your labels</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
        These recipes avoid wheat, barley and rye as they are written. What
        we can't check for you is the shopping: gluten hides in soy sauce,
        stock cubes and bouillon, gravy and onion soup mixes, malt vinegar,
        most oats, and plenty of seasoning blends. Brands change their
        recipes without telling anyone.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
        If you are coeliac, read the packet every time, and treat the notes
        on each recipe as the cook's best knowledge rather than a
        guarantee. If something here looks wrong to you, please tell the
        parish office — we would far rather fix it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</Layout>
